The retrieval architecture implemented here (inference-free learned sparse
retrieval, with document-side neural encoding and a static query weight table)
is the OpenSearch project's design. This repository contributes the embedded
SQLite implementation, the file format, the reference implementation and the
measurements, and redistributes converted copies of OpenSearch's models.

Third-party work, with provenance.

llama.cpp, https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp, MIT License.
  Compiled into the sparse0 extension (pinned commit in CMakeLists.txt) to run
  the document encoder. Also used, at commit c1d0e7a004015f23bc0233470b747b596f29b264,
  to convert the encoders below to GGUF with its convert_hf_to_gguf.py.

utf8proc, https://github.com/JuliaStrings/utf8proc, MIT License (Unicode data
  under the Unicode license). Compiled into the sparse0 extension for the query
  tokenizer's case folding, normalization and character categories.

