  What the redistributed files under https://huggingface.co/arbazsiddiqui contain
  and where each tensor came from.
  <model>_f16.gguf   The BERT encoder body of the checkpoint (embeddings,
                     attention and feed-forward layers, layer norms), converted
                     by llama.cpp's converter to GGUF at f16. No tensor was
                     added, removed or altered beyond the container change.
  <model>_q8.gguf    The same, quantized to Q8_0 by llama.cpp's llama-quantize.
                     Values change by quantization only.
  <model>.sprs       Tensors llama.cpp's converter omits, copied from the same
                     checkpoint without modification: the masked-LM head
                     (cls.predictions.transform.dense weight and bias, its
                     LayerNorm weight and bias, cls.predictions.bias), the
                     decoder weight (the word-embedding matrix, which the head
                     ties to), the model's static query weight table (the
                     SparseStaticEmbedding module), and the WordPiece
                     vocabulary from the checkpoint's tokenizer. Nothing in the
                     sidecar was trained, generated or reconstructed by this
                     project; the file is a serialization of existing tensors
                     plus a small header (format version, dimensions, an
                     activation flag that records which log1p variant the
                     checkpoint's pooling uses). Written by
                     bindings/python/sqlite_sparse/convert.py.
